+# FAA Tyson timeline, transcript and cassette-label crosswalk
+
+**November 9, 2026 | B129 / PD03–PD04 / PD07.** Five official National Archives PDFs add the contents of two Washington National Tower Tyson timeline scans, two related transcript editions, and cassette-label copies. They supply a candidate for the timeline and strips described by the September 16 fax, and separate paper records of transcription and rerecording scope. Exact fax payload, receipt, audio identity and continuity remain open.
+
+## Timeline and strip sheets
+
+Both **DCA-77** scans have three physical pages. The p. 1 heading identifies Washington National Tower, TYSON Departure Sector and **9/11/01**. The upper margin of both shows **“Original 9/16/01”** with initials. P. 2 is a continuation and p. 3 reproduces four marked strips. NAID **7596284** p. 1 has overlays covering portions of text and carries a note about a view without obscurities. In this particular entity the second physical page is the timeline's printed **Page 2**. The separately indexed **7596283** p. 1 presents the previously covered lines in view. Both scans have the same ordered lists of **22** and **17** extracted time labels on pp. 1 and 2. Their image layers, text readability and SHA-256 differ. The upper handwritten date remains an inscription. Its author, edition order and relationship to the fax are open. [Unobstructed copy](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/1-AAL-77/e-Other/1-DCA-77-TYSON-DEP-timeline-unobstructed.pdf) · [Other copy](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/1-AAL-77/e-Other/1-DCA-77-TYSON-DEP-timeline.pdf)
+
+DCA-51's cover describes **3 PAGES** of Tyson timeline and flight progress strips. Its separate confirmation row is dated September 16 and reports **004** pages. Shared description, date and three-page extent identify DCA-77 as a candidate. The first-page overlays, page sets and counts remain separately preserved. No transmitted page image, attachment ID or receiver copy identifies either scan as the payload. [DCA-51 field review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/9e8b75c1396cdd81b875d49098add254279dab11/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-aea-field-fax-trace-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+## Transcript comparison
+
+**DCA-53**, NAID 7596265, is a five-page table headed DCA-ATCT-AAL77. The finding aid classifies it as **Uncertified Transcript**. **DCA-61**, NAID 7596274, has a September 20, 2001 certification page and identifies the TYSON Departure Control position, accident file **ZDC-ARTCC-212**, and **1325–1348 UTC**. Five selected rows about the traffic advisory, aircraft-type estimate, follow instruction and two reported observations share the same second labels in both transcripts and both timelines, after removing colons for matching only. Source labels and exact locators are retained in the pins. These are document correspondences. They do not establish independent recording origins or clock accuracy. [DCA-53](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/1-AAL-77/e-Other/1-DCA-53-Uncertified-transcript.pdf) · [DCA-61](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/1-AAL-77/e-Other/1-DCA-61-TYSON-Departure-control-transcript.pdf)
+
+| Compared field | DCA-53 | DCA-61 | DCA-77 unobstructed |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Aircraft-down report | P. 4 line 27, **1338:00** | P. 7 line 23, **1338** | P. 2 line 20, **13:38:00** |
+| Climb and heading 330 instruction candidate | P. 5 lines 11–13, **1340:20** instruction and **1340:25** reply | P. 8 lines 26–29, **1340:20** instruction and **1340:25** reply | P. 2 line 39, **13:40:40** instruction summary |
+| End of the displayed texts | P. 5 lines 44–45, **1342:42** last displayed spoken entry and blank **1343:00** row | P. 9 lines 34–42, **1342:42** last displayed spoken entry and bare **1343–1348** labels, followed by **End of Transcript** | P. 2 ends with the **13:40:40** summary. |
+
+The climb instruction candidate is a comparison of similar displayed content. Whether the records refer to the same transmission is unverified. The aircraft-down and later Pentagon reports are communication entries with distinct labels. They leave the actual impact time and interval from event to report unmeasured. The transcript lines with no transcribed speech leave audio continuity, duration and omissions unresolved.
+
+## Labels and later certification
+
+**DCA-79**, NAID 7596285, preserves seven pages of **ORIGINAL** and **COPY** label images. Those words are printed on labels associated with the Commission rerecording paperwork. The label images establish the displayed labels. The underlying media and transmission history require separate proof. [DCA-79](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/1-AAL-77/e-Other/1-DCA-79-Cassette-tape-label-copies.pdf) · [DCA-23 certified index and routing](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/509f6490b9703e55ef57babf9a1040ba8c542102/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-october-tasking-potomac-copy-and-routing-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+- **TYSON.** DCA-79 p. 3 lines 18–19 and p. 4 lines 18–19 give **1324–1350 UTC** for TYSON COPY and ORIGINAL. The paired TYSON/ENSUE labels on p. 6 lines 18–20 repeat that Tyson range. DCA-23 p. 5 OCR line 42 gives the same range in its October 15 certified index. The October 22 slip on DCA-23 p. 1 OCR line 28 lists **1325–1348 utc** for Tyson radar position, matching the transcription window stated on DCA-61 p. 1 line 20. Preserve the two intervals and their source roles. No audio boundary was tested.
+- **TMCRA.** DCA-79 pp. 1–2 line 23 each give **1509–1513 UTC** for the third interval. On p. 5 line 12 both the ORIGINAL and COPY labels instead give **1509–1542 UTC**. The preceding **1350–1400 UTC** and **1427–1455 UTC** agree across the checked labels. DCA-23 p. 5 OCR lines 30–31 lists **1509–1542 UTC** in the certified index. Preserve the two endpoint labels and the 29-minute difference between their printed endpoints. No label version, tape side, substitution or cause was established.
+
+## Verification and open records
+
+All **27** pages in the five new PDFs were screened using their text layers. Visual checks covered the six timeline and strip pages, transcript certification and selected entries, selected label regions, and the held October routing slip and certified index. The reproducible comparison checks ordered label strings, five selected transcript/timeline row correspondences, and the distinct windows. Exact scans, hashes and conflict wording are retained. No audio or clock test was performed. [Source pins and checks](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+1. Find the actual DCA-51 fax image set and recipient-side intake to test the candidate DCA-77 join. Find DCA-52's inbound IAD/DCA delivery and itemized cassette manifest. The paper transcript and label matches do not identify the 2001 response or establish the completeness of a later production.
+2. Seek the original recorder/channel export, actual labeled cassettes or images of the carriers, rerecording work order, versioned labels and receiving copy. Join by position, date, side, interval and accession. The two TMCRA endpoints are unresolved.
+3. Continue the Eastern Region assessment and forwarding trace. The corrected May 2003 answer and receipt, signed decision and recommendation-specific dispositions remain priority originals.
